    "sha": "315089177fe1636ab5a8e40992246c4fdbd0c711",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVmlK7doAKDMxNTA4OTE3N2ZlMTYzNmFiNWE4ZTQwOTkyMjQ2YzRmZGJkMGM3MTE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-09T01:28:27Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-09T01:28:27Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): refuse carrying stock between setups on different machines\n\nThe program sim checked only the active setup's machine kind, so a carry\n(or clip) across a machine change was judged unrefused, against what the\n#401 notes said. The machine is now each setup's own (#343):\n\n- carry::entry refuses a carry onto another machine by name\n  (CARRY_MACHINE_REFUSAL, naming both setups and both machines), so the\n  rest reading (#318) refuses it at generation too; the lathe/mill-turn\n  gate reads the setups' shared machine instead of the active one's.\n- carry::walk (simulate_document, incoming_body) refuses every setup\n  change onto another machine, the M3.2 A clip included.\n\nPins carried-grid alignment for an odd cell count under an off-grid\ntranslation, in the engine (7 x 5 lattice, flip and quarter turn\ntranslated by (0.37, -1.13)) and in the app (a flip about a part centre\noff the grid pitch): every image cell centre is a transformed source\ncentre, origin and bounds exact, nothing shifted.\n\nDecisions: docs/decisions/404-carry-machine-check.md.\n\nFixes #404\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
